{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "class-crud-collection",
		"name": "Level 1 - Class CRUD (Depends: AcademicYear) - CORRECTED ENDPOINTS",
		"description": "Complete CRUD operations for Class model (Level 1 - Single Dependency)\n\n🔧 **Configuration:**\n- Base URL: http://127.0.0.1:8003\n- Authentication: Admin JWT Token (auto-fetched)\n- Tenant: test_tenant\n- Path: /api/v1/masters/class_sections/\n\n📋 **Dependencies:**\n- **Requires**: AcademicYear ID (from Level 0)\n- **Foreign Key**: academic_year_id → academic_years.id\n- **Nested Structure**: Optional sections array with SectionCreate objects\n- **Cascade**: Class deletion removes all sections\n\n📋 **12 Endpoints Covered (REAL endpoints, not API reference):**\n1. CREATE Class with Sections (POST /)\n2. GET Class by ID (GET /by_class_id/{class_id})\n3. LIST All Classes with Sections (GET /read_all)\n4. UPDATE Class (PUT /{class_id})\n5. DELETE Class (DELETE /{class_id})\n6. GET Class-Section List (GET /class-section-list)\n7. GET Classes Only (GET /class-list)\n8. GET Sections Only (GET /section-list)\n9. GET Sections by Class Name (GET /sections-by-class-name?class_name=)\n10. GET Classes Dropdown (GET /dropdown)\n11. GET Sections by Class ID (GET /by_class_id/{class_id}/sections)\n12. GET Students by Class-Section (GET /by-class-section?class_name=&section_name=)\n\n🎯 **Variable Chaining:**\n- Uses {{created_academic_year_id}} from Level 0\n- Auto-captures class_id for dependent requests\n- Chains nested sections creation\n- Complex class-section relationship handling\n\n⚠️ **Rate Limits:**\n- CREATE: 30 per minute\n- Dropdown operations: 100 per minute\n\n🎯 **Features:**\n- Nested sections validation\n- UUID format validation\n- Complex relationship testing\n- Comprehensive dropdown endpoints\n- Class-section filtering operations",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"auth": {
		"type": "bearer",
		"bearer": [{"key": "token", "value": "{{admin_token}}", "type": "string"}]
	},
	"event": [{
		"listen": "prerequest",
		"script": {
			"type": "text/javascript",
			"exec": [
				"// Auto-fetch admin token if not present",
				"if (!pm.globals.get('admin_token')) {",
				"    pm.sendRequest({",
				"        url: 'http://127.0.0.1:8003/api/v1/auth/test-jwt/admin-token',",
				"        method: 'GET'",
				"    }, function (err, response) {",
				"        if (!err) {",
				"            pm.globals.set('admin_token', response.json().access_token);",
				"            console.log('Admin token refreshed');",
				"        }",
				"    });",
				"}",
				"",
				"// Ensure AcademicYear dependency exists",
				"if (!pm.globals.get('created_academic_year_id')) {",
				"    console.warn('WARNING: academic_year_id not found. Run AcademicYear collection first!');",
				"}"
			]
		}
	}],
	"variable": [
		{"key": "base_url", "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8003", "type": "string"},
		{"key": "tenant_schema", "value": "test_tenant", "type": "string"}
	],
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "0. Get Admin Token",
			"event": [{
				"listen": "test",
				"script": {
					"exec": [
						"pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
						"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
						"});",
						"pm.test('Token received and stored', function () {",
						"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData.access_token).to.exist;",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData.user.role).to.eql('Admin');",
						"    pm.globals.set('admin_token', jsonData.access_token);",
						"    console.log('Admin token set for Class testing');",
						"});"
					]
				}
			}],
			"request": {
				"method": "GET",
				"header": [],
				"url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/test-jwt/admin-token",
				"description": "Get admin JWT token for authentication"
			}
		},
		{
			"name": "0.1 [DEPENDENCY] Create Academic Year for Testing",
			"event": [{
				"listen": "test",
				"script": {
					"exec": [
						"pm.test('Academic Year created successfully', function () {",
						"    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
						"});",
						"pm.test('Academic Year ID captured for dependency', function () {",
						"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData.id).to.exist;",
						"    pm.globals.set('created_academic_year_id', jsonData.id);",
						"    console.log('AcademicYear ID for Class dependency:', jsonData.id);",
						"    ",
						"    // UUID validation",
						"    var uuidRegex = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[1-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[89ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i;",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData.id).to.match(uuidRegex);",
						"});"
					]
				}
			}],
			"request": {
				"method": "POST",
				"header": [
					{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"},
					{"key": "cschema", "value": "{{tenant_schema}}"}
				],
				"body": {
					"mode": "raw",
					"raw": "{\n    \"title\": \"Class Dependency AY 2025-26\",\n    \"start_date\": \"2025-04-01\",\n    \"end_date\": \"2026-03-31\",\n    \"is_active\": true\n}"
				},
				"url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/masters/academic_years/",
				"description": "Create AcademicYear as dependency for Class testing"
			}
		},
		{
			"name": "1. CREATE Class with Sections",
			"event": [{
				"listen": "test",
				"script": {
					"exec": [
						"pm.test('Status code is 201 Created', function () {",
						"    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
						"});",
						"pm.test('Class created with proper structure', function () {",
						"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData.id).to.exist;",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData.name).to.exist;",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData.short_code).to.exist;",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData.academic_year_id).to.exist;",
						"    ",
						"    // Store for dependent requests",
						"    pm.globals.set('created_class_id', jsonData.id);",
						"    console.log('Created Class ID:', jsonData.id);",
						"    ",
						"    // UUID validation",
						"    var uuidRegex = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[1-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[89ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i;",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData.id).to.match(uuidRegex);",
						"});",
						"pm.test('Academic Year dependency correctly linked', function () {",
						"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
						"    var expectedAcademicYearId = pm.globals.get('created_academic_year_id');",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData.academic_year_id).to.eql(expectedAcademicYearId);",
						"    console.log('✅ Academic Year dependency verified');",
						"});",
						"pm.test('Sections created with class', function () {",
						"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
						"    if (jsonData.sections) {",
						"        pm.expect(jsonData.sections).to.be.an('array');",
						"        pm.expect(jsonData.sections).to.have.lengthOf(2);",
						"        console.log('✅ Sections created:', jsonData.sections.length);",
						"    }",
						"});"
					]
				}
			}],
			"request": {
				"method": "POST",
				"header": [
					{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"},
					{"key": "cschema", "value": "{{tenant_schema}}"}
				],
				"body": {
					"mode": "raw",
					"raw": "{\n    \"name\": \"Grade 10\",\n    \"description\": \"Tenth grade class\",\n    \"is_active\": true,\n    \"short_code\": \"G10\",\n    \"academic_year_id\": \"{{created_academic_year_id}}\",\n    \"sections\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"Section A\",\n            \"description\": \"First section\",\n            \"is_active\": true\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"Section B\",\n            \"description\": \"Second section\",\n            \"is_active\": true\n        }\n    ]\n}"
				},
				"url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/masters/class_sections/",
				"description": "Create Class with nested Sections and AcademicYear dependency"
			}
		},
		{
			"name": "2. GET Class by ID",
			"event": [{
				"listen": "test",
				"script": {
					"exec": [
						"pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
						"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
						"});",
						"pm.test('Class details returned correctly', function () {",
						"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData.id).to.exist;",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData.name).to.exist;",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData.academic_year_id).to.exist;",
						"    ",
						"    var expectedId = pm.globals.get('created_class_id');",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData.id).to.eql(expectedId);",
						"    console.log('Class details:', jsonData.name);",
						"});"
					]
				}
			}],
			"request": {
				"method": "GET",
				"header": [{"key": "cschema", "value": "{{tenant_schema}}"}],
				"url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/masters/class_sections/by_class_id/{{created_class_id}}",
				"description": "Get specific class by UUID (REAL endpoint path)"
			}
		},
		{
			"name": "3. LIST All Classes with Sections",
			"event": [{
				"listen": "test",
				"script": {
					"exec": [
						"pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
						"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
						"});",
						"pm.test('Response is array with sections', function () {",
						"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
						"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.be.an('array');",
						"    if (jsonData.length > 0) {",
						"        pm.expect(jsonData[0].id).to.exist;",
						"        pm.expect(jsonData[0].name).to.exist;",
						"        pm.expect(jsonData[0].academic_year_id).to.exist;",
						"        console.log('Classes with sections listed');",
						"    }",
						"});"
					]
				}
			}],
			"request": {
				"method": "GET",
				"header": [{"key": "cschema", "value": "{{tenant_schema}}"}],
				"url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/masters/class_sections/read_all",
				"description": "Get all classes with sections (REAL endpoint path)"
			}
		},
		{
			"name": "4. GET Class-Section List",
			"event": [{
